# Rendered by shellf per host. Its own placeholders are shown below, inside a verbatim
# region — a template can document what it carries (ADR-0049). Before that, this comment
# had to spell out "an at-sign and braces" in prose, because writing the marker asked
# shellf to substitute a variable that did not exist (#356, #481).
#
~{raw}
# A shellf placeholder looks like ~{name}. Anything between the raw markers is copied
# as-is: no substitution, no lookup, so an example costs nothing.
~{endraw}
#
# docker-compose's own ${...} is left untouched either way — that is why the sigil is
# neither `$` nor `{{`.
DOMAIN=~{domain}
DB_PASSWORD=~{db_password}
# compose reads ${DOMAIN} / ${DB_PASSWORD} below — passed through verbatim
VIRTUAL_HOST=${DOMAIN}
